Z||000000||yellowFormula||09-12-1999||10:15 PM||||Anyone ever tried to dye their seat covers? If so what did you use to do it and did it turn out as expected ? <P><BR>thanks, <BR>jeff <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/MotorCity/Track/3487" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/MotorCity/Track/3487</A> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||theogre||09-12-1999||10:28 PM||||you can't really dye them. The vynal won't take the fabric dye. The fabric won't like the dyes that will take on the vynal. the foam and gause under the fabric are also likely to do odd things if you get them really wet. Like mildew.<P>besides that, unless the fabric is in really good shape, its likely to fall apart.<P>I think you'd be better off finding either aftermarket replacements, or having new covers made by a good shop. You can get leather covers from MrMikes in a number of colors.||||reg||1
